# Python Notes — Integers, Floats & Arithmetic

## Integers and Floats

Integer (int) = a whole number.
Example: age = 16

Float (float) = a number with a decimal.
Example: price = 19.99

Use type() to check the type of a value.
Example: type(10) → int
Example: type(10.5) → float

## Arithmetic Operators

| Operator | Operation           | Example | Result |
| -------- | ------------------- | ------- | ------ |
| +        | Addition            | 5 + 2   | 7      |
| -        | Subtraction         | 5 - 2   | 3      |
| *        | Multiplication      | 5 * 2   | 10     |
| /        | Division            | 5 / 2   | 2.5    |
| **       | Exponent            | 5 ** 2  | 25     |
| %        | Modulus (remainder) | 5 % 2   | 1      |
| //       | Floor division      | 5 // 2  | 2      |



